<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Minh Mang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1791–1841</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Minh Mang was the second emperor of the Nguyen dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, ruling from 1820 to 1841. He centralised the administration on Chinese models, renamed the country Dai Nam and persecuted Catholic missionaries and converts. In 1832 he abolished the last autonomous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cham">Cham</a> principality of Thuan Thanh, ending the political history of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/champa">Champa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/minh-mang.jpg" alt="Minh Mang" width="320" height="498" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown, there is a line below the picture in the book that says: Drawn by a Chinese. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Minh_Mang.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
